# Test d'API SOAP avec TestCafe

## Introduction

TestCafe est principalement conçu pour les tests E2E UI, mais il peut aussi tester des API SOAP via des requêtes HTTP. Voici comment procéder.

## Installation

```bash
npm init -y
npm install testcafe --save-dev
npm install axios xml2js --save-dev
```

## Structure du projet

```
project/
├── tests/
│   ├── soap/
│   │   ├── soap.helper.js
│   │   ├── soap.test.js
│   │   └── soap.fixtures.js
├── package.json
└── .testcaferc.json
```

---

## 1. Helper SOAP (`soap.helper.js`)

```javascript
import axios from 'axios';
import xml2js from 'xml2js';

class SoapHelper {
  constructor(wsdlUrl) {
    this.wsdlUrl = wsdlUrl;
    this.headers = {
      'Content-Type': 'text/xml;charset=UTF-8',
      'SOAPAction': '',
    };
  }

  // Construire une enveloppe SOAP
  buildEnvelope(action, namespace, params) {
    const paramsXml = Object.entries(params)
      .map(([key, value]) => `<${key}>${value}</${key}>`)
      .join('');

    return `<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
      <soap:Envelope 
        xmlns:soap="http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
        <soap:Header/>
        <soap:Body>
          <${action} xmlns="${namespace}">
            ${paramsXml}
          </${action}>
        </soap:Body>
      </soap:Envelope>`;
  }

  // Envoyer une requête SOAP
  async sendRequest(soapAction, envelope) {
    try {
      const response = await axios.post(this.wsdlUrl, envelope, {
        headers: {
          ...this.headers,
          'SOAPAction': soapAction,
        },
      });

      return {
        status: response.status,
        data: response.data,
        parsed: await this.parseXml(response.data),
      };
    } catch (error) {
      if (error.response) {
        return {
          status: error.response.status,
          data: error.response.data,
          parsed: await this.parseXml(error.response.data),
          error: true,
        };
      }
      throw error;
    }
  }

  // Parser la réponse XML
  async parseXml(xmlString) {
    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
      xml2js.parseString(
        xmlString,
        { explicitArray: false, ignoreAttrs: true },
        (err, result) => {
          if (err) reject(err);
          else resolve(result);
        }
      );
    });
  }

  // Extraire une valeur du XML parsé
  extractValue(parsed, path) {
    const keys = path.split('.');
    let current = parsed;

    for (const key of keys) {
      if (current && current[key] !== undefined) {
        current = current[key];
      } else {
        return null;
      }
    }
    return current;
  }
}

export default SoapHelper;
```

